A||||5||Ed||No problems, good drive in the mountains||||1||
Z||000000||Ed||09-02-2001||01:34 AM||||We have a tendency here to mostly submit problems for repair advice.  But once in a while there's good news.  <P>Went for a two day drive in the Lake Tahoe area.  Nothing broke, the brakes worked fine, and people moved over and let me by.  The ignition module didn't fail, the car didn't overheat, the CD worked, the A/C worked, etc.  No noticeable bump steer. <P>So for some of you who are frustrated about your cars, take heart.  Sometimes everything works, and our "cheap" sportscars do what they're supposed to.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Urchin||09-02-2001||02:16 AM||||Good to hear.  I wish I could be so fortunate  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-02-2001||02:18 AM||||Amen to that!!  I had a nice ~200mile blast up and down the coast today, car worked *flawlessly* and the T-tops stayed off :) :) :)<P>Wind in your hair, engine humming up and down like a fine musical instriument, rowing through the gears with the glee of a child, the cobalt blue pacific ocean at your side and the slowly setting fiery auburn sun casting crysteline reys through the tender fog.<P>This is what sports cars are made for :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
